Wahzor wrote:
> Thanks for all the advice, especially about wielding stuff to uncurse
> it with a scroll of remove curse, it always bugged me that you couldn't
> uncurse regular inventory items with them.

You can wield whatever you want. So if your BoH is cursed you can wield 
it (it doesn't even weld in your hand) and read remove curse. Presto the 
BoH is uncursed. Remember to wield your normal weapon.

When you use commands that require you to select something from your 
inventory check the prompt. It's usually something like this (afG ?*). 
the a, f and G are those items that are implicitly connected to the 
command, ? gives you list of a, f and G so you can check which one you 
want to use and * gives your whole inventory.

That's how you wield cream pies, read T-shirts, throw tripe and do lot 
of more actions on items that aren't normally used with that action.

